WEBVTT

00:14.320 --> 00:16.360
I was shocked by his confidence.

00:16.400 --> 00:18.880
The best part was,
he spoke poker-faced,

00:19.480 --> 00:20.680
"Well, in that case,

00:20.920 --> 00:22.880
make me Titan's chairman."

00:23.000 --> 00:23.880
Did he?

00:24.520 --> 00:25.760
He... Come in.

00:25.960 --> 00:27.520
What confidence he had!

00:29.720 --> 00:30.760
'Gaurav Dhar.'

00:31.120 --> 00:31.920
Is it mine?

00:31.920 --> 00:33.080
But we'll have to
figure something out.

00:33.280 --> 00:35.160
Yes. Sir, the disparity
in numbers is quite large.

00:35.240 --> 00:37.120
- That's right.
- We must think of a solution.

00:40.720 --> 00:43.000
Oi! Are you getting married too?

00:44.720 --> 00:45.720
No...

00:46.200 --> 00:47.080
I mean...

00:48.480 --> 00:50.680
- Yes.
- Yes or no?

00:51.880 --> 00:52.960
Yes, sir.

00:53.440 --> 00:54.360
Really?

00:54.640 --> 00:56.880
That's great. Congratulations!

00:57.040 --> 00:58.520
Everyone seems to be
getting married.

01:14.600 --> 01:15.640
What is this?

01:17.000 --> 01:18.000
Everyone...

01:19.640 --> 01:21.080
Are you here to congratulate me?

01:26.480 --> 01:27.440
You know,

01:28.800 --> 01:29.880
Mom sent me

01:30.720 --> 01:32.880
photos of so many suitors

01:34.080 --> 01:36.280
and made me meet loads of boys,

01:37.400 --> 01:38.920
yet I didn't say yes.

01:39.960 --> 01:42.360
Who would agree
to marry such jokers?

01:46.440 --> 01:48.200
It's not your mother's fault.

01:49.440 --> 01:50.720
The suitors were just...

01:53.880 --> 01:55.280
In my tenement,

01:57.400 --> 01:58.520
everyone used to adore

01:59.320 --> 02:00.800
my father.

02:01.760 --> 02:03.720
Only Mom and I knew

02:04.080 --> 02:05.320
his reality.

02:07.760 --> 02:11.320
My mom would hear
everything he said quietly,

02:14.400 --> 02:15.680
but I was the opposite.

02:16.960 --> 02:19.560
That's why
I never got along with my dad.

02:21.440 --> 02:23.800
Over time, I became
convinced deep down

02:25.240 --> 02:27.880
that all men were like my father.

02:32.280 --> 02:33.720
And then I met you.

02:42.560 --> 02:44.560
Let me come
straight to the point, Gaurav.

02:50.440 --> 02:52.280
You are nice,

02:53.960 --> 02:55.160
different,

02:56.320 --> 02:57.720
and I like you.

03:00.040 --> 03:01.760
I don't want to delay any longer.

03:05.640 --> 03:07.880
I brought you this.

03:14.160 --> 03:17.200
Gaurav, shall we

03:18.560 --> 03:20.600
take care of each other for life?

03:47.040 --> 03:48.560
- Please eat.
- Should I?

03:58.040 --> 03:59.760
These 'laddus' are truly magical.

04:00.320 --> 04:01.280
Yes.

04:09.320 --> 04:12.120
- Congratulations, Gaurav and Megha.
- Thank you, sir.

04:12.160 --> 04:13.760
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

04:13.840 --> 04:15.400
I'm very happy for you two.

04:15.720 --> 04:17.200
I have some great news.

04:17.480 --> 04:19.600
You're late.
We've already heard the good news.

04:20.240 --> 04:21.040
How?

04:21.120 --> 04:22.280
They told us.

04:23.360 --> 04:24.880
How did you both find out?

04:25.520 --> 04:27.080
Of course, we know.

04:28.800 --> 04:30.840
Why wouldn't they know?

04:31.320 --> 04:32.400
Uh...

04:33.040 --> 04:33.840
What...

04:35.240 --> 04:37.960
Did you both find the solution
to internal smuggling?

04:38.040 --> 04:39.160
It's not that!

04:39.680 --> 04:41.120
They are marrying each other.

04:42.000 --> 04:42.840
Yes!

04:43.200 --> 04:44.480
Really!

04:45.040 --> 04:47.000
Okay! What a surprise!

04:47.040 --> 04:47.880
Yes, sir.

04:47.960 --> 04:49.320
Congratulations.

04:49.360 --> 04:50.320
Thank you, sir.

04:50.400 --> 04:52.200
- Congratulations, Gaurav.
- Thank you.

04:52.400 --> 04:53.440
What a surprise!

04:53.520 --> 04:56.240
Speaking of surprises...
Here! Catch it. Here!

04:56.800 --> 04:57.640
Here!

04:59.720 --> 05:01.840
So, 'Mr. Demonstration'.

05:02.960 --> 05:04.320
Will you please explain?

05:04.360 --> 05:07.080
Sure! These apples

05:07.400 --> 05:09.400
are bought from different states.

05:10.200 --> 05:11.880
It's the same apple,
with the same taste.

05:12.040 --> 05:13.720
But, Akash, your apple's price

05:13.760 --> 05:16.120
is two rupees more
than Gopalan's apple.

05:16.160 --> 05:16.920
Why?

05:17.040 --> 05:19.680
Because different states
levy taxes on them. That's why.

05:20.000 --> 05:20.800
Exactly!

05:20.800 --> 05:22.960
And the same thing
is happening to Titan.

05:24.160 --> 05:28.040
The Titan watch that sells
for Rs. 460 in Tamil Nadu

05:28.640 --> 05:31.280
costs Rs. 620

05:31.760 --> 05:34.240
in Mumbai

05:34.320 --> 05:35.960
because of various taxes.

05:36.720 --> 05:38.000
And people like Jaggu...

05:38.040 --> 05:40.680
They buy watches
at a lower price in Tamil Nadu

05:40.720 --> 05:43.240
and sell them in Maharashtra
at a lower price than us.

05:43.320 --> 05:46.640
- Exactly! - That's why
our sales are higher in the south

05:46.760 --> 05:47.760
than in the north.

05:47.840 --> 05:48.640
Man!

05:48.720 --> 05:50.840
Exactly!

05:50.920 --> 05:52.600
Despite the tax authorities,
the customs department,

05:52.680 --> 05:55.120
revenue officers, and the police,

05:55.400 --> 05:56.760
smugglers still manage
to smuggle goods

05:56.840 --> 05:58.280
in one way or another.

05:58.360 --> 06:00.240
And it's been happening
with many commodities.

06:00.280 --> 06:01.320
I did a little research.

06:01.360 --> 06:04.720
This is extremely concerning,
Mr. Desai.

06:04.760 --> 06:08.200
- It is!
- What's the solution then?

06:08.520 --> 06:09.520
UCP.

06:12.480 --> 06:13.320
Man!

06:14.000 --> 06:16.640
No! No! No, Mr. Desai.

06:16.920 --> 06:20.720
Implementing UCP in India
is next to impossible.

06:20.760 --> 06:21.480
Why?

06:21.520 --> 06:23.120
- UCP?
- Um.

06:23.480 --> 06:25.040
Uniform Consumer Price.

06:25.240 --> 06:26.920
Basically, it means

06:26.960 --> 06:29.280
that Titan watches will have
a uniform price across all states.

06:29.360 --> 06:32.360
Yes, we will take the prices from
25 states, calculate their average,

06:32.400 --> 06:34.400
and that will give us
our standard retail price.

06:34.520 --> 06:35.360
Okay.

06:35.400 --> 06:36.720
It's not that simple.

06:37.200 --> 06:38.920
It's not like a school exam.

06:39.360 --> 06:40.720
A big investment is involved here.

06:40.920 --> 06:43.880
And the states with lower tax rates

06:44.000 --> 06:46.520
will sell our watches
at a higher price.

06:46.600 --> 06:48.120
Yes, Mr. Gopalan, but the price

06:48.120 --> 06:49.640
will decrease in states
with higher taxes.

06:49.720 --> 06:52.200
Whichever side
you look at it from, Akash,

06:52.480 --> 06:53.840
we will incur a loss.

06:53.920 --> 06:55.400
Mr. Gopalan, you're

06:55.720 --> 06:57.920
thinking of selling
thousands of watches,

06:58.000 --> 06:59.200
whereas I want to sell
hundreds of thousands.

07:00.680 --> 07:03.280
Why don't you ever understand,
Mr. Desai?

07:03.400 --> 07:04.880
Besides the loss,

07:05.120 --> 07:06.280
if we fail,

07:06.920 --> 07:09.360
the state governments
will come after us.

07:09.400 --> 07:11.800
They'll think we're evading tax.

07:11.920 --> 07:13.760
If that happens,

07:13.840 --> 07:15.920
I'll take the responsibility.

07:16.400 --> 07:17.720
- What?
- Yes.

07:19.760 --> 07:22.480
Forget about profit
and loss for once.

07:23.840 --> 07:26.160
Is UCP beneficial

07:26.240 --> 07:29.200
for our consumers or not?

07:34.960 --> 07:36.120
I'm game for it.

07:37.680 --> 07:38.480
Yes.

07:39.040 --> 07:39.960
Then that's it.

07:40.040 --> 07:41.760
You'll be in big trouble, Mr. Desai.

07:41.840 --> 07:43.600
This is very risky.

07:44.120 --> 07:45.160
By the way, guys,

07:45.680 --> 07:47.440
marriage is risky too.

07:47.520 --> 07:48.760
Please ask Akash.

07:48.800 --> 07:49.600
Scary.

07:49.640 --> 07:51.360
Why are you scaring the poor things?

07:51.520 --> 07:53.240
Sir, did something happen
between you and Ms. Kumud?

07:54.040 --> 07:54.920
Everything will be good.

07:55.080 --> 07:56.560
- It's all good.
- It's scary.

07:56.600 --> 07:57.760
No, it's not like that.

08:18.800 --> 08:20.360
We don't just make watches,

08:20.560 --> 08:22.360
we do matchmaking too.

08:24.120 --> 08:25.080
Cheers, sir.

08:25.520 --> 08:27.040
What are you discussing?

08:27.560 --> 08:29.640
Did you know what they were up to?

08:30.000 --> 08:31.320
Yes, I did,

08:31.560 --> 08:33.280
but they realised late

08:33.480 --> 08:36.560
that they were made for each other.

08:41.560 --> 08:42.960
What are they discussing?

08:43.480 --> 08:44.880
Why don't you wear a watch?

08:45.640 --> 08:46.840
They are designed by you.

08:47.960 --> 08:49.960
Watches feel like handcuffs to me.

08:50.600 --> 08:51.720
And as a designer,

08:52.200 --> 08:53.720
I want my hands to be free.

08:55.440 --> 08:56.480
Perhaps they're saying

08:56.720 --> 08:59.840
that the two of us look good
together, like a dial and a strap.

09:12.760 --> 09:14.240
Is everything all right, Gopalan?

09:15.960 --> 09:20.040
I've been mulling something over
for the past few days, Mr. Desai.

09:20.320 --> 09:22.800
I can't keep it
to myself any longer.

09:22.960 --> 09:24.520
Is it about UCP?

09:24.560 --> 09:27.400
No. UCP is not a long-term solution.

09:27.520 --> 09:29.200
Smuggling will be controlled,

09:29.320 --> 09:31.520
but how will you increase the sales?

09:31.920 --> 09:33.640
And for that, you need to take

09:34.800 --> 09:36.320
some hard decisions, Mr. Desai.

09:38.080 --> 09:39.000
Such as?

09:39.680 --> 09:41.520
We've advanced from zero to ten.

09:41.600 --> 09:42.600
It's very good,

09:43.000 --> 09:44.920
but we need

09:45.360 --> 09:46.840
a fresh marketing perspective

09:47.480 --> 09:49.280
to become a hundred, you know.

09:50.120 --> 09:51.840
We need a...

09:52.000 --> 09:54.200
We need a fresh vision.

09:54.680 --> 09:55.920
I completely agree.

09:56.600 --> 09:58.240
I'll ask Megha to give us
some new ideas...

09:58.280 --> 10:00.360
No, that's not what I meant.

10:01.160 --> 10:02.160
Megha is good.

10:02.960 --> 10:03.880
She's good,

10:05.360 --> 10:06.240
but

10:07.160 --> 10:09.200
good is not enough, Mr. Desai.

10:10.760 --> 10:12.640
To be the best,

10:13.240 --> 10:14.920
we need someone experienced.

10:18.720 --> 10:21.080
- Are you asking me to fire Megha?
- No.

10:22.200 --> 10:23.360
We need

10:24.040 --> 10:27.120
an experienced addition to the team.

10:27.680 --> 10:29.320
Someone who knows

10:29.760 --> 10:33.160
how to build a brand from scratch.

10:35.560 --> 10:37.240
- Zee.
- Hmm?

10:37.720 --> 10:39.320
They're calling you two downstairs
for a group photograph.

10:39.480 --> 10:40.960
- Let's go.
- Coming!

10:42.000 --> 10:43.000
Hurry up.

10:45.760 --> 10:48.440
Anyway, will you think about it?

10:49.560 --> 10:50.400
Yes, sir.

11:00.360 --> 11:02.760
Hello, congratulations!

11:03.240 --> 11:05.000
The two of you
have been married today.

11:05.080 --> 11:06.040
I still can't believe this.

11:06.200 --> 11:07.880
It seems like it was just yesterday
when the ceiling fan fell.

11:08.720 --> 11:10.960
- Congratulations!
- Thank you, sir.

11:11.040 --> 11:12.080
Welcome!

11:12.480 --> 11:14.760
Thank God you've brought
a bouquet, not an envelope.

11:18.520 --> 11:19.360
Yes.

11:23.040 --> 11:25.240
Where are you going
on your honeymoon?

11:25.280 --> 11:26.760
We've chosen a lovely destination.

11:26.880 --> 11:27.960
- Huh?
- Hosur.

11:28.800 --> 11:30.440
I expected as much.

11:32.440 --> 11:33.280
What's this?

11:37.040 --> 11:39.120
Have you ever been to the Maldives?

11:45.440 --> 11:47.320
- Sir...
- Sir...

11:47.920 --> 11:48.840
It's my treat.

11:51.600 --> 11:53.640
- You deserve it.
- Thank you, sir.

11:53.720 --> 11:54.560
This...

11:54.760 --> 11:56.400
Congratulations, Gaurav.

12:04.640 --> 12:06.640
'To the brightest Titan'

12:11.960 --> 12:12.960
Thank you, sir.

12:13.280 --> 12:14.840
Congratulations, Megha.

12:19.280 --> 12:21.560
Oi! Are you crying?

12:22.520 --> 12:24.600
Mr. Desai praised you just now.

12:24.720 --> 12:25.520
- Okay.
- Rare...

12:25.840 --> 12:28.240
- That's rarest of the rare,
I would say. - Come on!

12:28.400 --> 12:29.960
Please come.
Let's have a group photo.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.800
- Mr. Gopalan, please come.
- Come on!

12:32.280 --> 12:33.880
- Pooja!
- Pooja, come here.

12:39.840 --> 12:40.640
Smile, please!

12:40.720 --> 12:41.800
- Smile!
- Smile!

13:05.760 --> 13:06.600
Jeh.

13:10.440 --> 13:11.520
What is it?

13:12.480 --> 13:13.440
Um.

13:13.920 --> 13:17.280
We must bring in
a new Head of Marketing.

13:17.800 --> 13:21.240
Someone who has launched
a couple of successful campaigns.

13:21.760 --> 13:23.200
Then please hire.

13:24.400 --> 13:25.200
Okay.

13:25.840 --> 13:28.760
By the way, whose idea was it?

13:29.200 --> 13:30.520
It was Gopalan's.

13:31.400 --> 13:32.280
I see.

13:33.720 --> 13:36.320
So, you've finally

13:36.520 --> 13:38.640
consulted the right person.

13:39.720 --> 13:40.520
Yes.

13:44.480 --> 13:45.720
Okay.

13:48.040 --> 13:49.080
Jeh.

13:50.360 --> 13:53.640
Are you determined
to bug the hell out of me today?

13:53.720 --> 13:55.600
Uh, no. Seriously.

13:55.840 --> 13:57.280
I need your advice.

13:58.280 --> 14:01.040
Megha has been with us
since the beginning.

14:01.280 --> 14:03.960
Yet I'm replacing her

14:04.480 --> 14:05.560
despite her loyalty.

14:05.680 --> 14:07.200
What's "nishtha"?

14:07.560 --> 14:08.520
Loyalty.

14:09.840 --> 14:11.320
Why did you do that?

14:12.280 --> 14:13.480
Because we need

14:13.680 --> 14:15.720
an experienced approach.

14:15.880 --> 14:17.280
She's talented,

14:17.640 --> 14:18.880
but she's young.

14:19.440 --> 14:21.600
She won't like this decision.

14:22.360 --> 14:23.800
Were you happy

14:23.920 --> 14:25.920
when you were sent to NBIDC?

14:26.000 --> 14:26.800
No.

14:26.920 --> 14:29.400
Yet you learned something more
than just improving your Hindi.

14:31.880 --> 14:32.720
Yes.

14:32.800 --> 14:34.080
Yes, so

14:34.240 --> 14:35.720
do you hate me?

14:36.360 --> 14:38.520
- No.
- Then shut up and let me play.

14:41.400 --> 14:43.120
All right. Here we go.

14:44.000 --> 14:46.400
All right.

14:51.480 --> 14:53.160
96!

14:53.240 --> 14:54.200
We only need one.

14:54.360 --> 14:56.080
- Yes, but not bad.
'- What?'

14:58.560 --> 15:00.080
'Couldn't you call me?'

15:04.640 --> 15:06.000
What's the matter, Akash?

15:08.640 --> 15:10.480
Did you send Megha on her honeymoon

15:10.560 --> 15:13.440
just to replace her
with a new Head of Marketing?

15:15.120 --> 15:16.040
No.

15:16.560 --> 15:18.120
That's not true, Akash.

15:21.600 --> 15:23.400
She'll be heartbroken, Zee.

15:26.880 --> 15:27.680
No.

15:30.480 --> 15:31.720
She'll understand.

15:33.840 --> 15:35.080
So you've already decided.

15:36.080 --> 15:36.920
Fine.

15:39.040 --> 15:42.480
Akash, you need to go to Hosur

15:42.800 --> 15:44.480
for a few days.

15:46.680 --> 15:48.080
- What?
- Hmm.

15:49.080 --> 15:50.240
I can't go there.

15:50.280 --> 15:51.520
They need me here more.

15:51.680 --> 15:53.200
Hear him out. He has a point.

15:53.840 --> 15:55.520
Don't misunderstand me, Akash.

15:55.920 --> 15:57.040
The sales are increasing,

15:57.680 --> 15:59.560
so we need someone
from the senior team

16:00.040 --> 16:04.120
to handle manufacturing, don't we?

16:06.400 --> 16:07.400
Oh.

16:08.280 --> 16:11.520
So, I'm being kicked out
of the head office.

16:14.360 --> 16:15.960
Fine. Not an issue. We'll see.

16:16.080 --> 16:16.880
Akash.

17:22.880 --> 17:25.120
It reminds us of both
the past and the present.

17:25.360 --> 17:26.840
We tweak it one way,

17:26.960 --> 17:28.000
you think Classique.

17:28.120 --> 17:29.960
- A tea, please. - When we
tweak it another way, we think...

17:30.040 --> 17:31.760
Sir, where is Titan's office?

17:34.680 --> 17:36.880
Young man, this sign

17:37.480 --> 17:39.040
is loud and clear.

17:39.840 --> 17:40.640
Ah!

17:43.640 --> 17:45.040
Why are you going there?

17:45.840 --> 17:47.160
I've come for an interview

17:47.840 --> 17:48.840
for the position
of Head of Marketing.

17:48.880 --> 17:49.960
I think you're late.

17:50.600 --> 17:51.800
Everyone has gone home.

17:53.120 --> 17:54.400
- Oh!
- Hmm.

17:57.160 --> 17:59.040
Okay. It's their loss.

18:00.240 --> 18:02.280
I had come
to change Titan’s destiny.

18:02.840 --> 18:03.680
How?

18:06.640 --> 18:07.880
Can you see that black scooter?

18:08.200 --> 18:09.160
Kinetic.

18:09.920 --> 18:12.280
It's expensive
and has very low mileage.

18:13.040 --> 18:15.400
But it's successful.
Do you know why?

18:16.160 --> 18:17.600
It has neither a kick-start
nor gears.

18:17.880 --> 18:19.400
And we marketed just that.

18:19.680 --> 18:20.920
The convenience.

18:21.880 --> 18:23.600
Now it's supremely popular

18:23.680 --> 18:25.440
with newlyweds and 'nearly deads'.

18:27.160 --> 18:29.000
Young couples and senior citizens.

18:29.240 --> 18:31.360
I realised something
while working at Kinetic.

18:31.720 --> 18:32.880
The product could be good,

18:32.920 --> 18:34.560
but the marketing
has to be even better.

18:36.200 --> 18:38.840
So you were

18:39.160 --> 18:41.920
- the Head of Marketing at Kinetic?
- Hmm.

18:42.400 --> 18:44.480
Kinetic is growing rapidly.

18:44.640 --> 18:46.080
Then why do you want

18:46.680 --> 18:48.080
to leave it and work for Titan?

18:49.160 --> 18:50.960
Kinetic is now on autopilot.

18:52.000 --> 18:55.040
It's time to help
a new Indian brand grow.

18:55.880 --> 18:57.080
I'd like that challenge.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.920
I can see a lack
of marketing insight at Titan.

19:01.600 --> 19:03.920
Maybe that's why
they are not flying.

19:04.760 --> 19:07.200
It's easy to say from the outside.

19:08.640 --> 19:10.400
I don't mind being an insider.

19:10.600 --> 19:12.400
Then come tomorrow
during office hours

19:12.760 --> 19:14.280
and meet Titan's MD.

19:17.840 --> 19:19.160
I'm meeting him right now, sir.

19:21.280 --> 19:23.280
You're the MD, Mr. Xerxes Desai,

19:23.360 --> 19:26.200
and you're the GM, Mr. Gopalan.

19:28.800 --> 19:29.640
And you?

19:31.920 --> 19:33.480
Murli Shankar Dalmia.

19:34.160 --> 19:36.240
People lovingly call me M.S.D.

19:36.480 --> 19:38.160
If you knew about the interview,

19:38.640 --> 19:39.920
why didn't you come earlier?

19:42.960 --> 19:46.400
What we can discuss
informally over tea

19:46.480 --> 19:49.400
cannot be discussed formally

19:50.120 --> 19:51.240
in a cabin, sir.

19:56.280 --> 19:57.240
Shall I give you my number,

19:57.280 --> 20:00.480
or will you look it up
in the directory?

20:00.960 --> 20:02.040
We'll look it up.

20:03.760 --> 20:04.800
I'll see you soon.

20:12.840 --> 20:15.800
It is very clear that we must
increase production capacity.

20:16.160 --> 20:18.960
If you need any help with this,
just let me know.

20:19.040 --> 20:19.840
- Sameer.
- Any help!

20:19.960 --> 20:20.960
He isn't making you
work too hard, is he?

20:21.000 --> 20:21.800
No, sir.

20:24.920 --> 20:25.760
How are you?

20:25.880 --> 20:27.560
Everything's going good.

20:27.640 --> 20:29.800
How does it feel to come straight
to work after your honeymoon?

20:30.080 --> 20:30.960
Uh...

20:32.160 --> 20:34.240
We already knew
about such challenges.

20:38.640 --> 20:40.440
Okay. I'll see you.

20:43.080 --> 20:43.880
Gaurav.

20:44.320 --> 20:45.160
Yes?

20:49.720 --> 20:50.920
Actually...

20:53.720 --> 20:55.360
They're hiring
a new Head of Marketing.

20:59.080 --> 20:59.880
Why?

21:04.080 --> 21:05.080
Megha...

21:06.160 --> 21:07.160
She'll understand.

21:08.560 --> 21:09.480
I hope so.

21:09.600 --> 21:10.720
Yes, she will.

21:13.040 --> 21:14.080
Hey!

21:14.440 --> 21:15.760
- Hello, sir.
- Hi, Megha.

21:15.800 --> 21:16.640
- Hi!
- Good morning.

21:16.680 --> 21:17.840
Morning! Morning...

21:18.000 --> 21:19.000
How was your trip?

21:19.480 --> 21:20.360
Very good, sir.

21:20.440 --> 21:21.920
That's good. Superb.

21:22.560 --> 21:24.280
We were waiting for you, Megha.

21:24.440 --> 21:25.440
Yes.

21:28.840 --> 21:30.480
Is everything fine, sir?

21:30.600 --> 21:33.320
- Everything's fine.
- Right. Um...

21:33.520 --> 21:36.760
There have been some developments
in your absence.

21:36.840 --> 21:39.880
- Positive developments, you know.
- Yes.

21:41.280 --> 21:43.040
So glad to find you both here.

21:43.480 --> 21:44.480
Hi...

21:49.760 --> 21:52.480
- Hi, I'm M.S.D.
- Megha Mhatre.

21:52.600 --> 21:53.840
Nice to meet you.

21:55.640 --> 21:57.680
Murli Shankar Dalmia.

21:57.880 --> 22:00.880
He's our new Head of Marketing.

22:07.680 --> 22:09.400
Murli, let's talk in my office.

22:09.600 --> 22:10.600
Yes? We'll take it there.

22:10.840 --> 22:12.320
- I'll leave it to you.
- Yes.

22:12.520 --> 22:13.840
- Thank you, Murli.
- See you, Megha.

22:14.680 --> 22:16.000
Yes, Megha. Take care.

22:20.760 --> 22:22.000
When was it decided?

22:22.880 --> 22:25.640
Only two people now know
the timing of decisions at Titan.

22:31.000 --> 22:32.880
And I'm not one of them anymore.

22:44.240 --> 22:46.320
- Sir, have I been fired?
- No. No! No!

22:46.480 --> 22:48.240
Not at all.

22:48.400 --> 22:50.480
Sir, is it because I'm married?

22:50.640 --> 22:52.320
No. Absolutely not.

22:53.200 --> 22:55.200
Then why are you demoting me, sir?

22:56.040 --> 22:57.440
You're not being demoted.

22:57.440 --> 23:01.000
But I'm no longer
the Head of Marketing.

23:05.280 --> 23:06.080
No.

23:09.760 --> 23:11.960
We needed help.

23:12.040 --> 23:13.920
Someone with experience

23:13.960 --> 23:16.080
in building a brand from scratch.

23:17.240 --> 23:18.680
You'll learn from him,

23:18.760 --> 23:20.840
and he'll learn from you.

23:21.360 --> 23:23.240
Because you know
the brand better than anyone.

23:25.600 --> 23:28.840
You're the first employee
of this company.

23:30.680 --> 23:31.520
Megha.

23:32.920 --> 23:33.960
Megha.

23:36.320 --> 23:38.440
You're my favourite person here.

23:41.000 --> 23:43.400
Thank you, sir.

24:01.160 --> 24:02.920
Do you think you've been replaced?

24:09.360 --> 24:11.520
You have a wall clock
in front of your desk, don't you?

24:12.960 --> 24:13.800
Hmm.

24:14.360 --> 24:15.640
Bring it to your desk.

24:16.040 --> 24:16.880
Why?

24:17.440 --> 24:19.200
Please bring it, Megha.

24:21.120 --> 24:22.000
Wait a minute.

24:31.560 --> 24:32.400
Yes.

24:34.400 --> 24:35.840
Did the presence of the wall clock

24:35.960 --> 24:37.440
make your wristwatch disappear?

24:39.560 --> 24:40.360
No.

24:41.920 --> 24:42.840
That's the point.

24:44.320 --> 24:45.960
A replacement

24:46.240 --> 24:48.120
replaces something old.

24:49.760 --> 24:51.120
'You're both there together.'

24:51.760 --> 24:53.160
So this is an enhancement.

24:53.320 --> 24:54.520
Yes, but Gaurav,

24:54.880 --> 24:57.360
I was a part of Titan
since it began.

24:57.440 --> 24:58.560
And you still are.

24:59.480 --> 25:01.040
No one can change that.

25:01.560 --> 25:03.360
'The Head of Marketing may change,'

25:03.880 --> 25:07.080
'but Megha Mhatre will always
be part of Titan's first batch.'

25:07.640 --> 25:09.400
You've seen the company
come to life.

25:09.680 --> 25:11.080
You've seen it grow.

25:13.760 --> 25:14.680
'Right?'

25:16.200 --> 25:18.160
M.S.D. is an experienced
professional, Megha.

25:18.840 --> 25:20.800
You can use this as an opportunity.

25:22.200 --> 25:23.520
You can learn from him.

25:25.080 --> 25:26.800
If things get worse,

25:27.680 --> 25:28.880
I'll teach you how to make watches.

25:29.040 --> 25:30.280
Then you can join
the Engineering Department.

25:33.720 --> 25:34.880
When are you coming home?

25:35.200 --> 25:36.640
I'll come tonight.

25:37.440 --> 25:38.240
Are you sure?

25:38.560 --> 25:40.120
Hmm. Sure.

25:40.760 --> 25:42.320
Okay. Bye.

25:42.640 --> 25:43.480
Bye!

26:09.120 --> 26:11.520
'Tata's Trust, Titan.'

26:11.840 --> 26:13.320
'India's Best Watch'

26:23.880 --> 26:25.040
Miss Megha.

26:25.280 --> 26:27.880
A tagline is the identity
of a brand,

26:27.920 --> 26:30.680
but if you keep changing it,

26:30.760 --> 26:33.960
how will consumers
recognise Titan, the brand?

26:37.160 --> 26:38.640
"Utterly butterly delicious!"

26:38.800 --> 26:40.960
What do you recall when I say this?

26:40.960 --> 26:42.240
Of course, Amul.

26:43.560 --> 26:44.880
"Someone who loves his wife..."

26:44.960 --> 26:46.800
"Cannot say no to Prestige."

26:48.120 --> 26:49.560
A tagline defines a brand.

26:49.840 --> 26:51.880
Do you think
people have been gifting diamonds

26:52.080 --> 26:53.880
since the Mahabharata?

26:56.920 --> 26:57.720
Anyone?

26:57.800 --> 27:00.160
Previously, diamonds
were used as investments,

27:00.360 --> 27:02.040
much like gold bars.

27:02.120 --> 27:04.360
Then De Beers launched a campaign.

27:04.920 --> 27:07.640
"A diamond is forever."

27:09.520 --> 27:13.040
That tagline transformed
the whole scenario.

27:14.600 --> 27:15.920
That's what I want for Titan.

27:16.000 --> 27:18.600
Sir, what are the things
we are trying to convey?

27:18.760 --> 27:20.120
Very good question to begin.

27:21.480 --> 27:24.440
- Quality.
- A brand by the Tatas, for sure.

27:25.360 --> 27:26.280
Quartz!

27:26.760 --> 27:27.920
Like a...

27:29.280 --> 27:31.240
A world-class watch

27:32.040 --> 27:33.640
with a wide range

27:33.720 --> 27:36.840
of designs and prices,

27:36.840 --> 27:39.200
from the house of the Tatas.

27:41.520 --> 27:43.240
Sir, we need a tagline,
not an essay.

27:45.000 --> 27:45.960
Okay.

27:48.320 --> 27:49.360
What about

27:49.680 --> 27:51.760
"Titan Quartz by Tatas"?

27:52.320 --> 27:53.120
It's simple.

27:56.280 --> 27:57.400
'Titan...'

27:59.200 --> 28:00.400
'Tatas...'

28:00.520 --> 28:01.640
It's quite direct.

28:06.040 --> 28:07.400
It is so direct

28:10.560 --> 28:11.840
that it is perfect.

28:14.520 --> 28:16.600
It's simple, clean,

28:17.240 --> 28:19.720
and elegant, just like the Tatas.

28:20.280 --> 28:22.880
Think about it.
It combines Titan's branding,

28:22.880 --> 28:25.480
Tata's trust,
and the curiosity of quartz.

28:29.120 --> 28:30.360
I think it's perfect.

28:31.000 --> 28:33.160
Comprehensive content
in just a few words.

28:34.360 --> 28:35.800
Yes, I think that's it.

28:36.320 --> 28:37.160
Well done.

28:39.440 --> 28:40.240
Hello!

28:41.200 --> 28:42.800
- How is everyone?
- Hi, sir.

28:43.040 --> 28:43.840
Akash?

28:44.320 --> 28:46.160
What about Hosur?

28:46.440 --> 28:47.680
Everything's fine in Hosur.

28:47.680 --> 28:49.840
I also had a word with Mr. Gopalan.

28:51.640 --> 28:54.520
I'll go there when they need me.

28:56.400 --> 28:57.400
Is it okay with you?

28:59.040 --> 29:00.120
Welcome back!

29:01.640 --> 29:02.560
Let me introduce you.

29:02.600 --> 29:04.040
Allow me to do it myself, sir.

29:06.000 --> 29:06.960
M.S.D., sir.

29:07.400 --> 29:08.200
Hi...

29:08.520 --> 29:09.400
"M.S.D.?"

29:09.560 --> 29:10.760
Murli Shankar Dalmia.

29:11.040 --> 29:12.480
Ah, nice. I'm Akash.

29:12.600 --> 29:13.400
I know.

29:13.560 --> 29:15.680
He is the new Head of Marketing
for Titan.

29:16.320 --> 29:17.840
Oh! That's nice.

29:19.160 --> 29:20.280
So he's already been hired?

29:22.560 --> 29:25.080
- Nice. Congratulations.
- Sir.

29:28.960 --> 29:29.840
Sir.

29:32.640 --> 29:34.960
- We'll have to do it again.
There's no shadow. - Boss!

29:36.240 --> 29:37.920
Allow me to introduce you
to someone.

29:38.000 --> 29:39.120
He is Suresh Malik.

29:39.200 --> 29:41.280
He has just come from Bombay.

29:41.600 --> 29:43.040
He's from the OBM agency.

29:43.080 --> 29:45.960
They have delivered the most
successful campaigns in our country.

29:46.120 --> 29:47.640
He'll work with us now.

29:47.800 --> 29:48.960
Lovely to have you on board.

29:49.080 --> 29:50.880
Mr. Xerxes Desai and Mr. Gopalan.

29:51.320 --> 29:52.920
- Good to have you.
- Welcome.

29:53.120 --> 29:55.160
Can we do... What time is it?

29:55.240 --> 29:56.240
- 4:30.
- 4:30.

29:56.360 --> 29:58.200
Can we meet at 6:30 in my office?

29:58.280 --> 29:59.280
- Absolutely.
- Yes? Huh?

29:59.400 --> 30:01.160
- I'll be here.
- Thank you!

30:01.760 --> 30:03.440
You both look like each other's
'before' and 'after'.

30:04.040 --> 30:05.560
And I'm the much later version.

30:05.680 --> 30:06.680
Let's go.

30:09.280 --> 30:10.440
- Skip?
- Yes.

30:11.000 --> 30:12.120
Just like this.

30:13.120 --> 30:14.240
What a joke!

30:14.560 --> 30:17.120
Mahesh, can you stand
with your hand in your pocket?

30:18.760 --> 30:19.840
This way!

30:45.280 --> 30:47.880
I'm good. You're finally back.

30:49.600 --> 30:50.800
- Son-in-law!
- Namaste!

30:51.400 --> 30:53.240
- Please come. May I?
- No, it's fine.

30:53.600 --> 30:54.720
Come inside.

30:55.920 --> 30:57.120
Please come.

30:58.760 --> 30:59.800
Please keep the change.

31:03.480 --> 31:04.720
When will you listen to me

31:05.000 --> 31:06.160
and stop doing this work?

31:06.760 --> 31:08.120
Can you leave Titan?

31:08.360 --> 31:09.240
No.

31:09.320 --> 31:12.040
Then how can I leave my work?

31:12.880 --> 31:14.520
Your company is your passion,

31:14.720 --> 31:16.560
and my work is mine.

31:17.720 --> 31:18.520
Okay.

31:18.520 --> 31:19.800
At least eat for now.

31:19.880 --> 31:20.920
'Kuwartj.'

31:21.760 --> 31:22.560
It's "z".

31:23.120 --> 31:24.640
'Kuwartz.'

31:24.720 --> 31:25.840
- Quartz?
- Yes.

31:26.200 --> 31:27.680
- Quartz.
- Quartz.

31:33.800 --> 31:34.600
Hello?

31:35.360 --> 31:36.320
Yes, sir.

31:36.960 --> 31:37.760
What?

31:39.640 --> 31:41.080
I don't understand, sir.

31:44.200 --> 31:46.280
Yes, it's a bit chunky.

31:46.720 --> 31:47.880
I liked it.

31:48.600 --> 31:50.920
Sir, M.S.D. has called you.

31:51.840 --> 31:52.640
Where?

31:52.720 --> 31:54.680
He has called you to a wedding.

31:55.160 --> 31:56.200
He said it's urgent.

31:56.720 --> 31:57.600
"A wedding?"

31:58.000 --> 31:58.800
Huh?

31:59.080 --> 32:01.000
Why is he acting like a third wheel
at someone's wedding?

32:01.680 --> 32:04.240
He also said you must bring a gift.

32:07.560 --> 32:09.520
What is he up to?

32:09.560 --> 32:10.920
Whose wedding is it?

32:11.080 --> 32:12.200
No idea, sir.

32:21.080 --> 32:24.080
Oh! Thank you for coming
on such short notice.

32:24.120 --> 32:25.480
Murli, what is this?

32:25.600 --> 32:27.840
Sir, the 'rasam' is really tasty.
Please have some.

32:28.080 --> 32:29.840
Okay, but why did you call us here?

32:30.000 --> 32:30.960
Exactly!

32:31.840 --> 32:32.920
Did you bring the gift?

32:33.080 --> 32:34.000
Yes.

32:35.960 --> 32:37.040
An envelope.

32:37.240 --> 32:38.360
Yes. What now?

32:38.880 --> 32:40.280
Sir, it's wedding season.

32:40.640 --> 32:41.800
And what happens during this season?

32:42.000 --> 32:42.960
There are either weddings

32:43.080 --> 32:44.840
or wedding anniversaries.

32:45.000 --> 32:46.600
And what does
the whole country give as gifts?

32:46.760 --> 32:47.760
An envelope.

32:47.960 --> 32:48.920
Exactly!

32:49.040 --> 32:50.200
Just as you've brought one.

32:51.600 --> 32:55.080
What if we replaced
this good old envelope

32:56.240 --> 32:57.880
with a Titan?

33:05.360 --> 33:08.160
That's a great idea, sir.

33:11.040 --> 33:11.920
Thank you very much.

33:12.720 --> 33:15.880
But we have to sell watches,

33:16.000 --> 33:17.120
not a wedding souvenir.

33:17.200 --> 33:18.800
We have to sell a wedding souvenir!

33:19.360 --> 33:20.680
Why do we give gifts?

33:20.840 --> 33:22.400
To convey an emotion.

33:22.680 --> 33:23.960
And in our country,

33:24.040 --> 33:26.160
weddings are the most
emotional events.

33:26.320 --> 33:28.680
We just have to connect
the emotions of a wedding

33:28.920 --> 33:31.080
to Titan's, and we'll have a winner.

33:31.160 --> 33:32.240
Let's create a campaign.

33:32.320 --> 33:35.720
Let's make Titan the best
wedding gift ever in India.

33:38.920 --> 33:39.960
I love it.

33:41.200 --> 33:42.280
Approved.

33:44.400 --> 33:45.960
By the way, whose wedding is it?

33:46.080 --> 33:47.960
Ramesh and Revati's.

33:49.480 --> 33:50.520
Who are they?

33:51.440 --> 33:52.560
I don't know.

33:56.360 --> 33:58.080
- You don't know?
- Excuse me!

33:58.440 --> 33:59.480
- I was just...
- What?

34:00.720 --> 34:02.800
I was just passing by.

34:05.440 --> 34:06.680
But there's no need
to be embarrassed.

34:06.760 --> 34:08.480
We have an envelope
as a wedding souvenir.

34:08.600 --> 34:11.360
We can give them money per plate,
and perhaps a little extra

34:11.520 --> 34:12.800
as a courtesy. They won't mind.

34:12.920 --> 34:14.960
All right, but you could have
said this at the office.

34:15.000 --> 34:15.800
Exactly.

34:16.680 --> 34:18.280
I have heard a lot about you, sir.

34:19.080 --> 34:20.920
"No discussion, only demonstration."

34:26.000 --> 34:26.960
- I'm out of here.
- Yes.

34:33.080 --> 34:35.680
'Sir, if you're okay with it,
then let me present...'

34:35.720 --> 34:36.840
Okay, guys, I'll make a move.

34:37.680 --> 34:39.360
Yes, Akash. We are leaving too.

34:39.400 --> 34:41.280
Just some last-minute discussions.

34:41.360 --> 34:43.120
- Sorry...
- If you like, I can wait a bit.

34:43.120 --> 34:44.600
- Not a big deal.
- No, Akash.

34:44.960 --> 34:46.800
Go home! You look tired.

34:47.720 --> 34:48.960
Please have some rest.

34:50.520 --> 34:52.840
Sir, we can also stay
if you'd like to discuss anything.

34:52.840 --> 34:55.120
Megha, office hours are over.

34:55.200 --> 34:56.560
Don't worry so much.

34:56.840 --> 34:59.480
We'll discuss it tomorrow morning
with a fresh mind.

35:00.480 --> 35:01.960
It's okay, Megha. We should leave.

35:02.760 --> 35:03.760
I guess

35:03.960 --> 35:06.720
some very important company
matters are being discussed here.

35:07.400 --> 35:10.640
It's okay, you may continue,
Mr. Gopalan and M.S.D.

35:11.240 --> 35:12.200
See you, guys.

35:16.240 --> 35:18.360
Sir, what is Akash's role
in this company?

35:21.920 --> 35:23.400
Sometimes he advises on sales,

35:23.520 --> 35:25.680
and at other times
on finance or logistics.

35:26.920 --> 35:29.200
I don't understand his actual role.

35:31.120 --> 35:32.440
Do you have a father, sir?

35:34.720 --> 35:35.640
What?

35:37.000 --> 35:38.040
Your father.

35:41.200 --> 35:42.040
Yes, I have.

35:42.200 --> 35:44.280
If you don't mind me asking,
what does he do?

35:46.080 --> 35:46.960
He was an engineer.

35:48.480 --> 35:49.560
What about your brothers
and sisters?

35:49.720 --> 35:51.240
- Gaurav.
- Just a minute.

35:52.800 --> 35:54.840
- I have a brother.
- Okay. What does he do?

35:55.160 --> 35:56.360
He's studying medicine.

35:56.920 --> 35:57.720
That's nice.

35:58.240 --> 35:59.360
What does your mother do, sir?

35:59.760 --> 36:00.560
She's a homemaker.

36:00.720 --> 36:02.760
No, I mean, what's her role?

36:06.440 --> 36:09.280
She does everything.
How can you define a mother's role?

36:10.400 --> 36:12.640
Right.
We cannot define a mother's role.

36:13.360 --> 36:14.480
That's what I mean.

36:14.560 --> 36:16.520
A mother is both a friend
and a teacher.

36:16.800 --> 36:18.880
If something goes wrong at home,
she takes care of it.

36:19.160 --> 36:21.040
She even manages
the household expenses.

36:22.840 --> 36:24.200
A mother does so much for us,

36:24.280 --> 36:25.720
yet we cannot define her role.

36:27.360 --> 36:28.480
What are we getting at?

36:29.200 --> 36:30.200
Akash...

36:34.120 --> 36:35.680
He is exactly the same with Titan.

36:38.280 --> 36:39.600
'Almost like a mother.'

36:41.920 --> 36:44.240
'He is also one of the founding
members of the company.'

36:45.440 --> 36:48.560
If you remove the mother from the
equation, the family won't survive.

36:55.320 --> 36:56.240
Shall we?

37:08.000 --> 37:10.240
I know you will end up choosing
either Terry Cotton or Terry Wool.

37:10.280 --> 37:11.840
Your entire wardrobe
is full of those.

37:12.000 --> 37:14.160
Which one was the woollen one?

37:14.920 --> 37:15.800
What was its name?

37:15.880 --> 37:17.440
- Merino?
- "Merino!" Merino wool!

37:17.520 --> 37:18.840
Please show me something
made of Merino wool.

37:18.960 --> 37:20.320
Okay, sir. Merino...

37:20.400 --> 37:21.680
This is a very fine fabric, sir.

37:21.760 --> 37:23.400
- Fine fabric...
- Yes, sir.

37:23.800 --> 37:25.600
No, show me something else.

37:25.680 --> 37:27.880
No, I don't like this.

37:27.960 --> 37:29.600
- Show me something else.
- Sir.

37:29.720 --> 37:31.120
- Anything else?
- This...

37:31.200 --> 37:33.120
Something softer...

37:33.240 --> 37:34.360
Not this.

37:34.440 --> 37:36.120
No, it's too rough.
Do you have it in another material?

37:36.200 --> 37:37.880
Sir, you yourself don't know
what you want.

37:39.200 --> 37:40.920
What should I show you then?

37:43.840 --> 37:44.640
Fine.

37:45.480 --> 37:46.360
Let's go, Raj.

37:49.040 --> 37:50.800
Do you know anything
about customer service?

37:52.560 --> 37:53.600
Yes? Good luck.

37:53.720 --> 37:55.360
Good luck with this guy.

37:59.600 --> 38:02.760
You're expecting
too many options from a shop.

38:02.840 --> 38:03.640
Yes.

38:04.600 --> 38:07.520
How many designs does Titan offer?

38:10.840 --> 38:11.680
Four?

38:13.920 --> 38:15.760
Aren't you being hypocritical?

38:19.040 --> 38:20.400
Yes, you're right.

38:21.760 --> 38:23.120
And I won't play it safe.

38:25.480 --> 38:27.240
Dangerous! Here!

38:27.840 --> 38:28.880
Dangerous!

38:32.520 --> 38:34.160
So you mean

38:34.320 --> 38:36.200
we should invest
more in watch designs?

38:36.280 --> 38:37.080
Yes.

38:37.960 --> 38:39.120
Honestly,

38:39.760 --> 38:41.760
our sales are barely increasing.

38:42.320 --> 38:45.560
We haven't even
fully recovered from UCP,

38:45.840 --> 38:47.920
and yet you want to offer
new designs to every customer.

38:48.000 --> 38:49.480
Not for every customer,

38:49.520 --> 38:51.960
but different options
for each type of customer.

38:52.000 --> 38:52.840
I got it.

38:53.760 --> 38:54.800
Indians love options.

38:54.880 --> 38:59.000
Mr. Desai, why do you
always come up with strategies

38:59.040 --> 39:00.720
that cause the company
to incur losses?

39:00.880 --> 39:04.040
This isn't the only area
we need to invest heavily in.

39:05.400 --> 39:07.000
What do you mean?

39:08.600 --> 39:09.560
M.S.D.

39:11.320 --> 39:12.800
Ladies and gentlemen,

39:13.760 --> 39:17.800
we are going to launch
our first TV commercial.

39:19.720 --> 39:21.320
What do you mean
by "we are going to"?

39:22.240 --> 39:23.920
When was this decided?

39:27.240 --> 39:28.960
Can you believe this?

39:29.720 --> 39:31.480
First, he shocked us
by talking about designs,

39:31.760 --> 39:33.760
and now it's the TV commercial.

39:33.880 --> 39:35.440
We have to do that, Akash.

39:35.560 --> 39:38.520
Your new ideas could
disrupt our accounts.

39:38.640 --> 39:40.360
How much more should we invest?

39:40.520 --> 39:43.320
If we don't invest,
how will we make a profit, Akash?

39:43.480 --> 39:46.240
If we fail, we'll sink, M.S.D.

39:47.160 --> 39:48.960
Our company
is making neither a profit

39:49.360 --> 39:51.040
nor do we have enough capital.

39:51.080 --> 39:53.160
And the campaign
you're talking about

39:53.280 --> 39:54.840
is even bigger than Bajaj's.

39:54.920 --> 39:55.720
Yes.

39:56.000 --> 39:58.640
This is bigger than even
the largest campaign in the country.

40:00.280 --> 40:02.280
He's got a valid point, Mr. Desai.

40:02.920 --> 40:03.720
Look.

40:04.840 --> 40:07.200
We want to establish our brand.

40:08.160 --> 40:09.040
Right?

40:09.720 --> 40:11.680
People don't go to a shop
and ask for toothpaste.

40:12.160 --> 40:13.320
They ask for Colgate.

40:14.160 --> 40:15.600
They don't want to get a photocopy.

40:15.840 --> 40:17.000
They ask for a Xerox.

40:17.320 --> 40:19.920
Similarly,
instead of asking for a watch,

40:20.600 --> 40:21.440
they should ask for Titan.

40:22.960 --> 40:27.160
- Look, Zee.
What you're saying is right. - Yes.

40:27.240 --> 40:28.520
- You're not wrong.
- Okay.

40:28.600 --> 40:30.200
But please slow down.

40:30.840 --> 40:33.240
You’re making an investment
of Rs. 80 lakh

40:33.360 --> 40:35.360
after sales of just Rs. 30 lakhs.

40:36.280 --> 40:38.240
This is not smartness,
but utter foolishness.

40:38.480 --> 40:39.680
Why should we stop, sir?

40:41.280 --> 40:43.440
All the other big brands

40:43.960 --> 40:45.920
are reaching every household
through television.

40:46.120 --> 40:49.440
Yet you want us to remain stuck
with just the hoardings.

40:49.560 --> 40:51.160
You need to understand one thing.

40:51.560 --> 40:54.120
Not every household
in this country has a television.

40:54.680 --> 40:57.240
Guys, we are not ready
to take such a big risk right now.

40:57.480 --> 41:00.800
If it fails, Titan will face
an unimaginable loss.

41:00.920 --> 41:02.800
If this campaign fails,

41:03.840 --> 41:05.920
I will tender my resignation.

41:08.000 --> 41:09.640
Mr. Desai,

41:10.560 --> 41:13.400
such a huge investment
on a single commercial?

41:13.560 --> 41:14.680
Why?

41:14.960 --> 41:17.520
I want Titan to reach
every household in this country.

41:18.320 --> 41:19.320
Every single household.

41:21.520 --> 41:24.880
How many states and regions
does our country have?

41:25.160 --> 41:27.600
Every state and region
has its own language.

41:27.760 --> 41:28.560
Correct.

41:28.680 --> 41:30.120
How many ads will you make?

41:30.200 --> 41:31.160
Absolutely right.

41:31.400 --> 41:33.440
We need something

41:34.960 --> 41:36.120
universal.

41:36.320 --> 41:38.720
Something that defines
the identity of Titan.

41:38.800 --> 41:39.840
Exactly.

41:43.480 --> 41:46.320
Sir, there is one thing

41:46.480 --> 41:48.240
that is universal

41:48.680 --> 41:50.480
and can reach every household.

41:53.200 --> 41:54.080
Music.

41:56.440 --> 41:57.760
Now we're talking.

41:59.960 --> 42:02.160
People might forget words,

42:02.280 --> 42:04.040
but tune...

42:05.440 --> 42:07.040
- Melody!
- Melody!

42:07.400 --> 42:08.280
"Nirma!"

42:08.520 --> 42:10.200
- "Washing powder Nirma."
- "Washing powder Nirma."

42:10.400 --> 42:11.960
- "Washing powder Nirma."
- "Washing powder Nirma."

42:12.000 --> 42:12.840
You know it.

42:12.840 --> 42:14.040
And Bajaj, sir.

42:14.240 --> 42:15.240
- Bajaj.
- Bajaj.

42:15.640 --> 42:19.600
"A magnificent image
of magnificent India!"

42:19.720 --> 42:21.560
"Our Bajaj!"

42:21.640 --> 42:23.640
"Our Bajaj!"

42:23.800 --> 42:26.200
"Our very own Bajaj!"

42:26.280 --> 42:27.080
Yes!

42:27.680 --> 42:29.240
Shall we, team?

42:31.360 --> 42:34.680
If it fails, you'll be free
of me and my nonsense.

42:36.720 --> 42:38.360
Mr. Desai...

42:39.000 --> 42:40.720
Huh? Gopalan?

42:42.400 --> 42:44.080
Megha? Gaurav?

42:46.240 --> 42:47.720
Akash...

42:49.640 --> 42:50.480
What?

42:50.720 --> 42:51.800
Say, "seri".

42:55.040 --> 42:58.160
[in Tamil] Just let it be.

42:58.680 --> 43:01.440
- "What else are we going to be?"
- That was a good idea, Megha.

43:02.600 --> 43:03.600
Thank you, sir.

43:04.360 --> 43:05.800
- Hi, Reshma!
- Hi.

43:05.880 --> 43:07.760
This is Titan's new watch,
for which we are shooting.

43:07.880 --> 43:09.800
The gift will be
placed on the table.

43:10.000 --> 43:11.040
You'll check it.

43:11.520 --> 43:12.960
That's it! That's what we want.

43:13.240 --> 43:14.320
We're good to go.

43:20.040 --> 43:21.680
- Well, the visuals are great.
- Yes.

43:22.880 --> 43:24.960
But the music...

43:25.520 --> 43:26.840
- It doesn't connect.
- Tsk!

43:30.720 --> 43:31.680
Let's find something.

44:18.080 --> 44:19.080
Did you find anything?

44:22.160 --> 44:23.000
Sorry.

44:24.160 --> 44:25.000
Did you find anything?

44:26.000 --> 44:26.800
No.

44:55.400 --> 44:56.800
What is this?

44:57.360 --> 44:59.800
Has Titan become
a music company now?

45:00.560 --> 45:02.640
Jeh, how come you're here?

45:03.840 --> 45:07.360
Yes, I came to attend a concert,
but the flight landed early.

45:07.960 --> 45:09.960
I thought I'd come and meet you all.

45:11.960 --> 45:13.320
There's a concert
going on here as well.

45:13.920 --> 45:14.720
No.

45:14.760 --> 45:15.880
No...

45:16.480 --> 45:17.720
We were just

45:18.360 --> 45:19.720
working on the campaign.

45:19.960 --> 45:23.760
Why does everyone look
so tired and lifeless?

45:24.880 --> 45:26.200
Come on. Come along with me.

45:27.280 --> 45:28.280
Call everyone.

45:32.240 --> 45:33.400
Ladies and gentlemen,

45:33.520 --> 45:36.560
presenting Mozart's 25th symphony.

47:35.480 --> 47:36.720
'Dad.'

47:38.920 --> 47:41.880
'Titan:
the most precious gift of love.'

47:57.320 --> 48:00.120
Dad, I want the watch
with that music.

48:04.360 --> 48:06.600
Although it's a foreign tune,
it connects so well.

48:06.960 --> 48:07.920
Shall we try a variation?

48:08.080 --> 48:09.080
What variation?

48:09.600 --> 48:11.000
Let's Indianise it.

48:13.760 --> 48:14.600
Hmm.

48:34.320 --> 48:36.080
Um, boss, there are only four boxes.

48:36.600 --> 48:37.680
We can load them into the car.

48:38.160 --> 48:39.360
We don't need a truck anymore.

48:41.960 --> 48:45.120
Sorry!
I'll load them onto the truck.

48:45.560 --> 48:46.480
Just a minute.

48:47.080 --> 48:47.960
Yes, boss?

48:48.240 --> 48:49.320
Show me your hand.

49:05.320 --> 49:06.520
Idiot!

49:08.320 --> 49:09.800
'Xerox' Desai,

49:11.360 --> 49:12.840
you've ruined my business.

49:54.960 --> 49:56.240
'Titan Quartz.'

49:57.080 --> 49:58.280
Whoa, Zee!

49:59.880 --> 50:00.920
You did it!

50:01.240 --> 50:04.880
You've delivered this symbol
to every single household in India.

50:05.640 --> 50:06.440
Thank you!

50:06.640 --> 50:07.680
Thank you, Jeh!

50:08.640 --> 50:11.520
Now, it's time for you

50:12.280 --> 50:14.640
to wear this symbol of excellence.

50:28.800 --> 50:30.040
Not yet, Jeh.

50:30.240 --> 50:33.080
This is India's best watch,
not the world's.

50:37.720 --> 50:39.240
There's still a long way to go.

51:02.880 --> 51:05.840
Titan has only eight months left.

51:07.280 --> 51:09.320
After that, our company

51:10.000 --> 51:13.440
might shut down permanently.

51:16.840 --> 51:17.840
I'm sorry.

51:25.200 --> 51:26.080
It's over.
